WEBVTT

00:36.258 --> 00:41.378
[10 Years Ago]

00:41.378 --> 00:43.735
[Episode 2]

00:55.842 --> 00:57.717
Excuse me.

01:05.128 --> 01:06.528
Um...

01:08.034 --> 01:09.952
Ms. Shibasaki?

01:23.170 --> 01:24.422
Darn it!

01:24.422 --> 01:25.965
Comrade Black Pearl,

01:25.965 --> 01:28.442
your mouth's gotten a lot dirtier
since I last saw you.

01:35.349 --> 01:37.159
Bulgae.

01:38.060 --> 01:41.246
You punk...

02:23.938 --> 02:25.792
[Lifeboat]

02:37.536 --> 02:39.846
Hands up and stand up slowly.

02:47.463 --> 02:50.091
I'd heard the rumors,

02:50.091 --> 02:52.401
but I never knew Bulgae was a woman.

02:53.010 --> 02:54.762
Quit screwing around

02:54.762 --> 02:56.571
and hand over the bag.

03:23.833 --> 03:25.642
Check the bathroom.

03:31.799 --> 03:34.276
- Boss?
- Yeah?

03:38.242 --> 03:39.648
Darn it.

03:41.016 --> 03:42.017
- Gong Bok.
- Yes.

03:42.017 --> 03:44.228
You keep an eye on these guys
and search every room.

03:44.228 --> 03:45.829
Yes!

03:46.522 --> 03:48.415
What are you waiting for? Hand it over.

04:55.549 --> 04:57.134
Who the heck are you?

04:57.134 --> 04:58.302
You're a man?

04:58.302 --> 05:00.429
So your eyes aren't
completely useless after all.

05:00.429 --> 05:02.473
Aren't you North Korea's top agent?

05:02.473 --> 05:03.891
What's with that? That's disgusting!

05:03.891 --> 05:06.227
Don't you know what a disguise
for an operation is?

05:06.227 --> 05:08.771
Even for an operation, that's too much.

05:08.771 --> 05:11.842
Darn it, whenever you lift your legs...

05:14.235 --> 05:16.737
I can't exactly fight with my eyes shut.
Man, that's disgusting.

05:16.737 --> 05:18.864
At least shave those legs!

05:18.864 --> 05:21.007
You are fighting with your mouth?

05:21.617 --> 05:24.427
Quit yapping and come at me.

05:48.104 --> 05:49.480
Darn it.

06:42.856 --> 06:44.096
No!

07:35.042 --> 07:37.227
You rat!

08:04.738 --> 08:05.906
What are you doing?

08:05.906 --> 08:08.008
Pull me up quickly!

09:26.536 --> 09:28.123
What... what are you?

09:28.123 --> 09:29.974
What are you, you punk?

09:31.272 --> 09:32.392
Darn you!

09:33.336 --> 09:34.937
Let go!

09:41.096 --> 09:42.376
[To. Heo Nam Il, 64 Hakun-ro, Yeongcheon-gun]

09:46.141 --> 09:48.159
Come on!

09:49.269 --> 09:51.271
Hey, you punk!

09:51.271 --> 09:52.997
Hurry.

10:36.776 --> 10:39.048
[Imcheon District Prosecutors' Office]

10:44.074 --> 10:46.201
There's only this CCTV footage

10:46.201 --> 10:49.204
on the USB you gave me, ma'am.

10:49.204 --> 10:53.057
A passenger ferry in 2016.

10:56.169 --> 10:58.896
I think this article is
from around the same time.

10:59.547 --> 11:02.300
Both the footage here and the gun.

11:02.300 --> 11:03.760
[Two NIS agents vanished]
Who exactly was this woman?

11:03.760 --> 11:05.053
[during a ferry arrest operation]
Why would she build a secret room

11:05.053 --> 11:06.346
just to hide all this?

11:06.346 --> 11:08.515
She definitely wasn't an ordinary civilian.

11:08.515 --> 11:10.392
That handgun found in that room

11:10.392 --> 11:13.728
is a Russian-made pistol
used by North Korean soldiers.

11:13.728 --> 11:15.271
Are you saying the dead woman was

11:15.271 --> 11:17.707
- Shh!
- a North Korean soldier?

11:20.360 --> 11:21.778
Why would someone like her

11:21.778 --> 11:23.838
commit suicide in South Korea?

11:24.489 --> 11:26.116
Rather than suicide,

11:26.116 --> 11:27.534
it's more reasonable to believe

11:27.534 --> 11:29.494
she was murdered
after her identity was exposed

11:29.494 --> 11:31.371
because of that NewTube video.

11:31.371 --> 11:33.540
It felt like she was living in hiding.

11:33.540 --> 11:35.375
Secretly

11:35.375 --> 11:38.211
while looking into the materials
we have here.

11:38.211 --> 11:39.295
First,

11:39.295 --> 11:42.132
let's find out who the people
in the CCTV footage are.

11:42.132 --> 11:44.175
We'll start by obtaining
the passenger list from that ferry.

11:44.175 --> 11:45.401
Yes.

11:49.806 --> 11:51.808
Yes, this is Prosecutor Kang Young Ae.

11:51.808 --> 11:53.409
Yes, Chief.

11:54.769 --> 11:56.245
Right now?

11:56.980 --> 11:58.273
Prosecutor Kang.

11:58.273 --> 11:59.858
Are you in your right mind?

11:59.858 --> 12:01.443
You've barely been here,

12:01.443 --> 12:03.278
and you've already reopened

12:03.278 --> 12:05.113
a suicide case on your own

12:05.113 --> 12:07.115
and visited the scene?

12:07.115 --> 12:08.950
If you stir things up like that,

12:08.950 --> 12:10.994
it's our hotshot prosecutor

12:10.994 --> 12:13.121
making the cops on the front lines

12:13.121 --> 12:15.097
do all the running around!

12:16.332 --> 12:18.559
Don't you know there'll be
talk behind our backs?

12:20.503 --> 12:22.104
No, sir.

12:23.840 --> 12:25.775
I didn't know.

12:27.844 --> 12:30.472
You didn't know?

12:30.472 --> 12:32.348
I'm so sorry, I failed

12:32.348 --> 12:34.450
to read the situation again.

12:35.477 --> 12:37.979
I got carried away with my enthusiasm

12:37.979 --> 12:40.482
and caused concern, and I sincerely

12:40.482 --> 12:42.083
apologize.

12:42.734 --> 12:45.570
Whether it's a written reprimand
or a pay cut, I'll take

12:45.570 --> 12:47.463
full responsibility.

12:49.532 --> 12:51.034
I'll let it slide this time

12:51.034 --> 12:53.953
and take the blame myself.

12:53.953 --> 12:55.497
But if I hear

12:55.497 --> 12:57.582
you're poking around

12:57.582 --> 13:00.293
in this case again,

13:00.293 --> 13:03.922
I'll ship you off to some
remote district office, got it?

13:03.922 --> 13:05.481
Yes, sir.

13:12.847 --> 13:15.350
I've made sure she won't get

13:15.350 --> 13:17.785
anywhere near the case again.

13:20.522 --> 13:22.440
[Chief Prosecutor Choi Byeong Guk]
Looks like

13:22.440 --> 13:25.151
the new one was a little too eager.

13:25.151 --> 13:26.986
Are you sure?

13:26.986 --> 13:28.279
Yes, sir.

13:28.279 --> 13:31.574
We've already coordinated
everything with the police,

13:31.574 --> 13:34.760
so what could possibly go wrong now?

13:35.828 --> 13:39.832
I'd like to meet you in person
and at least treat you to a meal,

13:39.832 --> 13:41.376
but I'm tied up with the campaign right now.

13:41.376 --> 13:43.044
Instead,

13:43.044 --> 13:45.839
I'll have Chief Baek
send my regards this evening.

13:45.839 --> 13:47.439
Yes.

13:54.055 --> 13:55.682
Representative Kim Joong Hyuk is here.

13:55.682 --> 13:56.933
Yeah, show him in.

13:56.933 --> 13:58.617
Yes, sir.

14:00.562 --> 14:02.397
Wow,

14:02.397 --> 14:04.874
what a view!

14:05.692 --> 14:08.152
The view of Imcheon City from up here

14:08.152 --> 14:10.822
is quite spectacular.

14:10.822 --> 14:12.548
I'm glad you think so.

14:14.242 --> 14:17.474
[Saehanjin Party Floor Leader,
Kim Joong Hyuk]

14:18.329 --> 14:22.792
But now that I'm standing here,

14:22.792 --> 14:26.687
there's one thing I don't understand.

14:28.131 --> 14:30.049
Why is the great Han Kyung Wook

14:30.049 --> 14:32.802
so determined to move into

14:32.802 --> 14:34.178
that old city hall building

14:34.178 --> 14:36.931
instead of staying here
with a view like this?

14:36.931 --> 14:38.808
What's there to gain

14:38.808 --> 14:40.893
from being the mayor of a small-town city?

14:40.893 --> 14:42.770
Especially when Kim Seon Jung

14:42.770 --> 14:44.856
has a firm grip on Imcheon City

14:44.856 --> 14:46.691
in this election.

14:46.691 --> 14:49.277
If you're willing to walk away

14:49.277 --> 14:51.029
from the easy road

14:51.029 --> 14:54.157
and jump into a messy election fight,

14:54.157 --> 14:58.411
there must be a reason for it, no?

14:58.411 --> 15:01.205
Why don't we sit down
and discuss it over tea?

15:01.205 --> 15:03.724
We just got something good in.

15:04.792 --> 15:06.419
Come on.

15:06.419 --> 15:09.631
Do you think you're the only one
asking me to sit down for tea

15:09.631 --> 15:11.299
during election season?

15:11.299 --> 15:12.884
Answer my question first.

15:12.884 --> 15:15.386
Then I'll decide
whether to have tea with you.

15:15.386 --> 15:17.388
Wow.

15:17.388 --> 15:20.449
I can't even begin to
keep up with your foresight, sir.

15:22.435 --> 15:24.020
Sir, have you ever

15:24.020 --> 15:25.938
heard of Yeongseondo Island?

15:25.938 --> 15:27.649
Yeongseondo Island?

15:27.649 --> 15:29.817
So you're saying you started all this

15:29.817 --> 15:31.110
over a single island?

15:31.110 --> 15:33.696
Let me make this easier
for you to understand.

15:33.696 --> 15:35.031
Please, have a seat.

15:35.031 --> 15:36.532
Yeongseondo Island

15:36.532 --> 15:38.493
is somewhat distant from the mainland,

15:38.493 --> 15:41.329
but it's strategically positioned

15:41.329 --> 15:42.664
for maritime trade

15:42.664 --> 15:45.249
with major Northeast Asian countries
like China and Japan.

15:45.249 --> 15:46.918
Its tourism potential isn't bad, either.

15:46.918 --> 15:48.711
The only thing holding it back

15:48.711 --> 15:50.630
is all the regulations,
environmental rules, protections for locals,

15:50.630 --> 15:53.383
and a whole bunch of other restrictions.

15:53.383 --> 15:54.717
Because of those regulations,

15:54.717 --> 15:57.512
there's only one casino
for locals operating right now.

15:57.512 --> 15:58.846
But what do you think would happen

15:58.846 --> 16:00.890
if wealthy foreign investors
were allowed to do business

16:00.890 --> 16:02.350
without all those restrictions,

16:02.350 --> 16:03.977
and if we loosened some rules

16:03.977 --> 16:05.645
and looked the other way on others?

16:05.645 --> 16:08.731
It wouldn't take much for
Yeongseondo Island to become

16:08.731 --> 16:10.733
the biggest entertainment hub in Asia.

16:10.733 --> 16:12.860
Has it already started?

16:12.860 --> 16:15.780
For tourism developers across Northeast Asia,

16:15.780 --> 16:17.156
Yeongseondo Island

16:17.156 --> 16:18.825
is the ideal location for a business base.

16:18.825 --> 16:19.951
A number of companies

16:19.951 --> 16:22.245
have already expressed
interest in joining the project.

16:22.245 --> 16:24.247
Selling off parcels of the island

16:24.247 --> 16:27.625
could generate roughly
25 trillion won in revenue.

16:27.625 --> 16:30.461
25 trillion won?

16:30.461 --> 16:31.587
With that kind of money,

16:31.587 --> 16:35.717
it could certainly serve as
a stepping stone for you

16:35.717 --> 16:37.719
to become President in four years, right?

16:37.719 --> 16:41.071
Do you really think
it'll go according to plan?

16:41.071 --> 16:43.850
Kim Seon Jung won't be easy to handle.

16:43.850 --> 16:46.227
If you lend your support, wouldn't things

16:46.227 --> 16:48.579
go much more smoothly?

16:49.954 --> 16:51.604
Well.

16:53.901 --> 16:56.195
Ah, right. Is that tea ready?

16:56.195 --> 16:58.380
You said something good came in?

17:06.205 --> 17:09.459
This is a bronze ewer
that Kim Jong Il sold to China

17:09.459 --> 17:11.518
during the Arduous March.

17:12.128 --> 17:14.005
I happened to acquire it through a connection

17:14.005 --> 17:15.673
during my time with the NIS.

17:15.673 --> 17:17.133
If it's all right with you,

17:17.133 --> 17:20.136
I'd like to give it to you as a gift.

17:20.136 --> 17:21.820
Would you accept it?

18:03.679 --> 18:06.432
This is the woman Mr. Kim Joong Hyuk
has been seeing recently.

18:06.432 --> 18:09.102
He secretly transferred a three-story
café building in Gangnam to her,

18:09.102 --> 18:11.745
and it appears there was
tax evasion involved.

18:14.899 --> 18:17.318
We'll need this if we're going to
keep that old man on a leash.

18:17.318 --> 18:18.986
- Keep it safe.
- Yes, sir.

18:18.986 --> 18:20.321
By the way,

18:20.321 --> 18:22.865
how's the land acquisition on
Yeongseondo Island coming along?

18:22.865 --> 18:24.450
The locals are putting up strong resistance,

18:24.450 --> 18:25.827
so things are moving slower than expected.

18:25.827 --> 18:27.411
Yoo In Goo went down there himself
to handle it.

18:27.411 --> 18:29.956
- Just give us a little more time.
- Joong Gi.

18:29.956 --> 18:32.124
You're talking too much.

18:32.124 --> 18:33.725
Huh?

18:34.961 --> 18:36.337
I'm sorry, sir.

18:36.337 --> 18:38.689
I'll order them to push forward
as aggressively as possible.

18:46.806 --> 18:50.601
Man, I told you we'd stamp the seal
and finish it, so why are you like this?

18:50.601 --> 18:52.562
That's our family burial ground.

18:52.562 --> 18:54.647
I said absolutely not...

18:54.647 --> 18:56.941
This guy still doesn't get it.

18:56.941 --> 18:59.402
I-I'll pay back

18:59.402 --> 19:01.696
the money I borrowed this week.

19:01.696 --> 19:03.364
- Please...
- Looks like he still needs more beating.

19:03.364 --> 19:04.965
Teach him a lesson.

19:06.492 --> 19:08.286
Everything going smoothly?

19:08.286 --> 19:10.162
Oh, boss!

19:10.162 --> 19:11.581
You should've called before coming.

19:11.581 --> 19:12.665
What brings you here so suddenly?

19:12.665 --> 19:14.834
I figured I should take some action too.

19:14.834 --> 19:18.045
Mr. Han is applying a lot of pressure,
demanding that we accelerate things.

19:18.045 --> 19:19.755
Boss, you can count on us.

19:19.755 --> 19:21.173
Zone A should be wrapped up soon.

19:21.173 --> 19:22.675
Well, looks that way.

19:22.675 --> 19:23.759
You're doing what you're told, right?

19:23.759 --> 19:25.778
Of course, boss.

19:28.162 --> 19:29.384
Yeah.

19:42.856 --> 19:44.872
[Jin Beef Jerky]

19:47.533 --> 19:51.136
Wow, the jerky business
is thriving these days, huh?

19:52.121 --> 19:53.581
But boss, is it really okay

19:53.581 --> 19:55.666
to run side businesses
behind the scenes like this?

19:55.666 --> 19:58.210
Mr. Han isn't exactly
someone to underestimate.

19:58.210 --> 20:00.087
Hey, that guy's too busy

20:00.087 --> 20:03.049
riding around in campaign trucks
giving speeches to notice.

20:03.049 --> 20:06.218
Once we take over Yeongseondo Island,
we'll all get our cut anyway.

20:06.218 --> 20:08.820
I'm just worried we might be
stirring up trouble for no reason.

20:09.430 --> 20:11.390
What a loyal dog.

20:11.390 --> 20:13.017
Once Yeongseondo Island
is taken over, you'll see.

20:13.017 --> 20:15.311
Do you really think Mr. Han, that snake,
and Chairman Do, that sly fox,

20:15.311 --> 20:18.230
are going to reward their underlings
for doing a good job?

20:18.230 --> 20:19.482
If anything, we'll be lucky

20:19.482 --> 20:21.317
if they don't just pick a fight
and beat us down.

20:21.317 --> 20:23.069
Before that happens,

20:23.069 --> 20:25.821
we need to take everything we can get

20:25.821 --> 20:27.615
if we don't want to end up
being used and discarded.

20:29.283 --> 20:30.785
I didn't realize there was
that much behind it.

20:30.785 --> 20:32.620
Boss!

20:32.620 --> 20:34.846
There's a problem with Capital.

20:57.687 --> 20:59.288
What's this?

20:59.897 --> 21:01.665
Ugh, my arm...

21:04.777 --> 21:06.753
Why can't I move my arm?

21:08.280 --> 21:10.199
Uncle, Uncle!

21:10.199 --> 21:12.680
Are you alright?

21:14.036 --> 21:15.496
Shouldn't you be lying down a bit longer?

21:15.496 --> 21:17.598
When...

21:18.708 --> 21:20.767
did I get home?

21:21.752 --> 21:23.421
I remember

21:23.421 --> 21:25.881
going to find the house deed

21:25.881 --> 21:27.425
and getting beaten up.

21:27.425 --> 21:30.052
Uncle, don't worry about the house deed.

21:30.052 --> 21:32.154
I've already secured everything.

21:33.889 --> 21:35.474
These punks

21:35.474 --> 21:37.059
really seem determined to squeeze

21:37.059 --> 21:39.244
every last drop out of the people
of Yeongseondo Island.

21:40.456 --> 21:42.356
[Certificate of Registered Matters (Full)]

21:42.356 --> 21:44.499
How did you get this back?

21:45.317 --> 21:46.918
Huh?

21:47.611 --> 21:48.754
Don't you remember?

21:49.655 --> 21:51.256
No.

21:53.576 --> 21:56.595
I remember getting hit.

21:57.246 --> 21:59.348
But after I got hit...

22:02.168 --> 22:04.295
What happened after that?

22:07.423 --> 22:08.799
My muscles are sore.

22:08.799 --> 22:11.218
Did I get beaten that badly?

22:11.218 --> 22:12.720
Uncle!

22:12.720 --> 22:15.614
Getting beaten isn't the issue right now.

22:16.348 --> 22:18.075
But

22:18.976 --> 22:21.437
why are you calling me "Uncle"?

22:21.437 --> 22:24.264
- Not "you," "hey," or "mister"?
- Jeez.

22:24.982 --> 22:28.794
I didn't know you well
at the time, that's all.

22:29.987 --> 22:32.782
Wow, I seriously felt like I was
watching a martial arts movie.

22:32.782 --> 22:34.992
T-This is me?

22:34.992 --> 22:36.285
Yeah!

22:36.285 --> 22:38.621
Your eyes suddenly went fierce,

22:38.621 --> 22:40.873
and then,

22:40.873 --> 22:44.351
you were mumbling something
and then just wiped them all out.

22:45.586 --> 22:47.479
I don't remember any of that.

22:48.923 --> 22:50.132
You're not lying to cover up

22:50.132 --> 22:51.801
what you did, are you?

22:51.801 --> 22:52.968
Come on.

22:52.968 --> 22:55.638
Why would I make up something like that?

22:55.638 --> 22:57.364
Take a look again. Huh?

23:00.935 --> 23:02.144
Huh?

23:02.144 --> 23:03.145
Is it me?

23:03.145 --> 23:04.939
I think when you got in danger,

23:04.939 --> 23:08.317
your hidden past came out.

23:08.317 --> 23:10.444
- Hidden past?
- Yeah.

23:10.444 --> 23:12.321
You know, like in the movies.

23:12.321 --> 23:13.906
When the hero's in danger,

23:13.906 --> 23:17.493
their past suddenly flashes back!

23:17.493 --> 23:20.262
Uncle, don't you remember anything?

23:20.996 --> 23:22.931
I just have a headache.

23:23.874 --> 23:25.126
I did

23:25.126 --> 23:27.503
some reasoning myself.

23:27.503 --> 23:29.672
"So who exactly are you, Uncle?"

23:29.672 --> 23:31.690
"How are you this good at fighting?"

23:32.883 --> 23:35.719
The answer came to me.

23:35.719 --> 23:37.763
Agent 007!

23:37.763 --> 23:39.223
And I didn't say it before,

23:39.223 --> 23:40.975
but I always thought

23:40.975 --> 23:43.577
you had that sharp, intense aura.

23:45.354 --> 23:47.748
Well, I suppose I do have that side to me.

23:50.359 --> 23:52.736
Is it that obvious even to you?

23:52.736 --> 23:55.005
Yes, it is!

23:56.323 --> 23:58.450
Bulgae has appeared! Bulgae!

23:58.450 --> 24:00.661
Ho Myung, calm down a bit.

24:00.661 --> 24:02.621
Oh, Seong Wo,
run this motorcycle plate for me.

24:02.621 --> 24:04.748
Well, it's in Imcheon, Yeongseon Ga...

24:04.748 --> 24:06.125
Uh, 9342!

24:06.125 --> 24:07.334
- Hey, Jeong Ho Myung!
- No, forget it.

24:07.334 --> 24:08.836
Come down now. Let's search together.

24:08.836 --> 24:10.754
We need to be careful
when things are urgent, man!

24:10.754 --> 24:13.482
Have you already forgotten
what happened ten years ago?

24:15.176 --> 24:16.385
Ho Myung,

24:16.385 --> 24:18.929
I'll give you the plate results
by tomorrow morning.

24:18.929 --> 24:20.389
First you need to check

24:20.389 --> 24:22.057
whether that guy is really Bulgae

24:22.057 --> 24:23.976
and whether he has the real item, okay?

24:23.976 --> 24:25.186
I'll wrap things up here

24:25.186 --> 24:26.504
and head right over.

24:26.504 --> 24:28.689
Okay? Stay calm.

24:28.689 --> 24:31.124
- Alright.
- Yeah.

24:32.318 --> 24:34.361
That's my guy Jeong Ho Myung!

24:34.361 --> 24:35.696
Sir!

24:35.696 --> 24:37.948
How much longer do I have to wait?

24:37.948 --> 24:40.326
Oh, yes, coming right away.

24:40.326 --> 24:42.578
- Oh my, really...
- Sorry.

24:42.578 --> 24:43.944
How long do I have to wait

24:43.944 --> 24:46.014
[Imcheon District Prosecutors' Office]
just for ice cream, seriously?

24:50.544 --> 24:52.046
Get out!

24:52.046 --> 24:54.506
Sorry, boss. I messed up, boss!

24:54.506 --> 24:56.608
- I'll do...
- Get out.

25:00.054 --> 25:01.180
Oh, wait a minute, wait!

25:01.180 --> 25:03.390
- Seriously...
- Get over here, you idiot. You're hurt now?

25:03.390 --> 25:05.142
It really hurts so much, it really does.

25:05.142 --> 25:06.952
That spot he hit earlier still hurts bad.

25:06.952 --> 25:08.562
I feel like I'm dying.

25:08.562 --> 25:11.148
You blew all the house deeds
and land deeds we worked so hard to collect,

25:11.148 --> 25:12.775
and you're complaining about pain?

25:12.775 --> 25:15.527
I'm telling you, he was seriously not normal!

25:15.527 --> 25:16.946
He was

25:16.946 --> 25:18.822
flying around,

25:18.822 --> 25:19.907
like a martial arts master.

25:19.907 --> 25:22.117
And that guy with the cap,

25:22.117 --> 25:24.328
his hands and feet were insanely fast.

25:24.328 --> 25:27.623
Man, I couldn't believe guys like that
would be in a backwater place like this.

25:27.623 --> 25:29.041
R-Really...

25:29.041 --> 25:30.709
What are you doing,
writing a restaurant review?

25:30.709 --> 25:31.877
No...

25:31.877 --> 25:33.254
- How many stars?
- Well, several.

25:33.254 --> 25:34.588
You little...

25:34.588 --> 25:38.050
You idiots, if you got beaten,

25:38.050 --> 25:39.927
you should've kept video

25:39.927 --> 25:41.095
or pictures of those punks' face.

25:41.095 --> 25:43.389
But you know, boss.

25:43.389 --> 25:45.182
Our CCTV is all just for show.

25:45.182 --> 25:47.351
Don't you remember you personally

25:47.351 --> 25:49.812
ordered us not to install CCTV at Capital

25:49.812 --> 25:51.605
to avoid any trouble down the line?

25:51.605 --> 25:54.566
Oh, right. So it's my fault?

25:54.566 --> 25:56.209
- Get over here.
- Yes, sir.

25:58.237 --> 25:59.905
Wait a second... it really hurts.

25:59.905 --> 26:01.736
I'm really sorry.

26:04.034 --> 26:05.536
Everyone get up!

26:05.536 --> 26:07.784
What do I do?

26:11.542 --> 26:13.168
- Hey!
- Yes.

26:13.168 --> 26:15.129
Talk to the hotel security team

26:15.129 --> 26:17.089
and get the lobby CCTV footage.

26:17.089 --> 26:19.091
Quietly, and Chairman Do mustn't know.

26:19.091 --> 26:20.926
W-Why can't we tell Chairman Do?

26:20.926 --> 26:22.928
Idiot. Is your brain not working or what?

26:22.928 --> 26:24.722
Chairman Do, that sly fox,
is already desperate to catch us.

26:24.722 --> 26:27.057
If he finds out about this mess,

26:27.057 --> 26:28.767
do you think he'll leave us alone?

26:28.767 --> 26:30.102
And if word about any trouble

26:30.102 --> 26:31.437
at the business even reaches Mr. Han,

26:31.437 --> 26:33.371
we're done for, don't you get it?

26:34.982 --> 26:36.317
Within three days,

26:36.317 --> 26:38.777
bring those guys to me.

26:38.777 --> 26:40.237
Be it martial arts master
or baseball cap guy,

26:40.237 --> 26:41.697
I'll deal with them myself.

26:41.697 --> 26:43.407
Yes, understood, boss.

26:43.407 --> 26:45.075
Answer him, you punks!

26:45.075 --> 26:46.785
- Yes, boss!
- Yes, boss!

26:46.785 --> 26:48.787
But, boss...

26:48.787 --> 26:50.513
Where should we go to look for them?

26:52.624 --> 26:54.418
Should I set your navigation for you?

26:54.418 --> 26:55.753
- Sorry!
- What are you waiting for?

26:55.753 --> 26:57.479
Move it!

26:57.479 --> 26:58.881
Ugh... hurry up!

26:58.881 --> 27:01.258
- Hurry.
- Idiots!

27:01.258 --> 27:02.312
It's true!

27:02.312 --> 27:05.153
[Enjoy the refreshing taste with Jumbo]
The Capital guys were beaten to a pulp.

27:06.013 --> 27:07.014
So?

27:07.014 --> 27:08.557
What do you mean "so"?

27:08.557 --> 27:09.892
He's someone who hasn't even gotten

27:09.892 --> 27:11.226
a single speeding ticket in 10 years.

27:11.226 --> 27:13.812
There's definitely a reason he made a move.

27:13.812 --> 27:15.439
Let's put him under 24-hour surveillance

27:15.439 --> 27:16.440
and dig into this properly.

27:16.440 --> 27:19.985
If we do 24-hour surveillance,
what about the 24-hour convenience store?

27:19.985 --> 27:21.236
Well, we'll just have to close it.

27:21.236 --> 27:22.237
Good, I was

27:22.237 --> 27:24.323
bored out of my mind anyway.

27:24.323 --> 27:25.366
Gong Bok.

27:25.366 --> 27:27.336
So you are late for your shift
because you were

27:27.336 --> 27:28.424
wandering around doing useless things?

27:28.424 --> 27:30.412
Does shift timing matter right now?

27:30.412 --> 27:31.663
That guy made a move!

27:31.663 --> 27:33.916
The one we've been watching for 10 years!

27:33.916 --> 27:37.044
Our boss is wrongly imprisoned,
and our scattered brothers...

27:37.044 --> 27:38.664
This could be our chance
to fix everything at once!

27:38.664 --> 27:39.752
Why are you hesitating?

27:39.752 --> 27:41.632
No, I'm asking why he suddenly moved?

27:41.632 --> 27:42.792
There's no reason!

27:42.792 --> 27:44.968
That's exactly why I'm saying
we should find out!

27:44.968 --> 27:47.528
You were never hesitant before.
Why are you acting like this?

27:49.218 --> 27:50.761
Oh, it's...

27:50.761 --> 27:53.280
It's because of that female cop, right?

27:54.348 --> 27:55.949
What?

27:57.310 --> 27:59.432
No, I mean...

27:59.432 --> 28:01.795
Well, I...

28:04.108 --> 28:06.152
Jeez, you.

28:06.152 --> 28:07.320
You.

28:07.320 --> 28:08.988
Where in the world does a part-timer

28:08.988 --> 28:10.756
monitor the boss like this?

28:11.908 --> 28:13.910
What did you say? Part-timer?

28:13.910 --> 28:15.369
Yeah.

28:15.369 --> 28:17.246
So I'm just a convenience store
part-timer here?

28:17.246 --> 28:19.332
Yeah.

28:19.332 --> 28:21.083
I understand how you feel, boss.

28:21.083 --> 28:22.418
But Jeong Ho Myung...

28:22.418 --> 28:23.878
Even if I have to do it alone,

28:23.878 --> 28:25.854
I'll tail him closely.

28:27.592 --> 28:28.633
Fine.

28:28.633 --> 28:29.992
Okay, go ahead.

28:29.992 --> 28:31.010
Go ahead, yeah!

28:31.010 --> 28:32.512
Hey, pay for that before you go!

28:32.512 --> 28:35.139
No, don't go! You need to take over my shift!

28:35.139 --> 28:37.741
I just pulled an all-nighter!

29:36.867 --> 29:38.886
Nice shot!

29:50.056 --> 29:51.080
Yes, Mr. Kim.

29:51.080 --> 29:52.675
I just sent you a license plate number.

29:52.675 --> 29:53.968
Yeah.

29:53.968 --> 29:56.278
I have one more favor to ask.

29:56.278 --> 29:58.952
[O Ran Chinese Restaurant]

30:11.152 --> 30:13.362
No news of Ho Myung yet?

30:13.362 --> 30:16.115
He doesn't have the guts
to collect unpaid bills anyway.

30:16.115 --> 30:19.343
It'd be lucky if he didn't get
beaten up by those thugs.

30:22.408 --> 30:23.980
- Oh!
- Oh!

30:25.750 --> 30:27.209
Looks like they didn't beat you up.

30:27.209 --> 30:28.377
Why didn't you answer your phone?

30:28.377 --> 30:29.420
What about the debt?

30:29.420 --> 30:31.339
Did they pay?

30:31.339 --> 30:33.132
I'm a bit tired,

30:33.132 --> 30:35.176
so I'll go upstairs and rest.

30:35.176 --> 30:36.777
No, wait...

30:43.142 --> 30:44.477
See?

30:44.477 --> 30:46.745
It was too much for Mr. Jeong, right?

30:51.592 --> 30:52.652
Jeez...

30:52.652 --> 30:54.904
If a man goes out with that much spirit,

30:54.904 --> 30:58.199
he should bring back at least
one ten-thousand won bill.

30:58.199 --> 31:01.285
Dad, don't you know him at all?

31:01.285 --> 31:04.413
From now on, never take orders
from Heaven Capital.

31:04.413 --> 31:05.456
Understood?

31:05.456 --> 31:06.457
Yeah.

31:06.457 --> 31:07.464
- Sir!
- Yes.

31:07.464 --> 31:09.393
- Got it?
- Got it.

31:20.471 --> 31:22.973
We need to be careful
when things are urgent, man!

31:22.973 --> 31:25.534
Have you already forgotten
what happened ten years ago?

31:27.395 --> 31:29.128
Go to Yeongseondo Island
and just find Bulgae, got it?

31:29.128 --> 31:30.248
Find Bulgae no matter what.

31:30.248 --> 31:31.524
It's dangerous for you to go alone.

31:31.524 --> 31:33.096
- Seong Wo, I'll go with you...
- No, don't come.

31:33.096 --> 31:36.028
Don't come and stay hidden
until I contact you, got it?

31:36.028 --> 31:37.379
I'll reach out.

32:00.010 --> 32:01.887
Han Kyung Wook!

32:01.887 --> 32:04.724
How dare you call your superior by name?

32:04.724 --> 32:07.435
Have you forgotten the chain of command?

32:07.435 --> 32:09.576
Han Kyung Wook, you punk!

32:09.576 --> 32:11.058
No!

32:19.947 --> 32:23.242
Even the righteous Mr. Cho is helpless.

32:23.242 --> 32:26.470
You're trembling over a few measly bullets.

32:28.330 --> 32:30.583
I'll give you a chance to live.

32:30.583 --> 32:31.917
You guys know

32:31.917 --> 32:33.919
where the item is, right?

32:33.919 --> 32:36.422
Did Jeong Ho Myung go look for it?

32:36.422 --> 32:38.023
Why?

32:40.259 --> 32:42.178
Even the mighty Han Kyung Wook

32:42.178 --> 32:43.820
is getting scared, huh?

32:46.056 --> 32:47.516
Okay, fine.

32:47.516 --> 32:50.144
Well, if I call Jeong Ho Myung
and ask him directly,

32:50.144 --> 32:51.353
I'll get my answer.

32:51.353 --> 32:52.646
Alright.

32:52.646 --> 32:54.690
Good luck finding him.

32:54.690 --> 32:57.693
You trained him yourself,
so you should know him well, right?

32:57.693 --> 32:59.487
Of course, I know

32:59.487 --> 33:02.490
what kind of guy Jeong Ho Myung is.

33:02.490 --> 33:03.783
That guy is

33:03.783 --> 33:07.302
top-tier in terms of skill,

33:08.621 --> 33:11.473
but he's too soft-hearted for his own good.

33:15.294 --> 33:18.422
If Jeong Ho Myung's respected senior,

33:18.422 --> 33:21.759
Mr. Cho Seong Wo, is said to be dead,

33:21.759 --> 33:23.219
he will definitely

33:23.219 --> 33:25.721
show up at the funeral.

33:25.721 --> 33:27.364
Don't you think?

33:36.148 --> 33:38.192
It seems the counterintelligence agents
have arrived.

33:38.192 --> 33:39.876
We should evacuate now, sir.

33:44.114 --> 33:45.115
Pull out for now.

33:45.115 --> 33:47.535
Deploy agents to the places they might go.

33:47.535 --> 33:49.136
Understood.

33:54.500 --> 33:57.002
This time, I won't let him escape.

33:57.002 --> 33:58.562
Not a chance!

33:58.562 --> 34:01.290
[NIS Agent Disappearance
Exposes Lapses in Internal Security]

34:22.600 --> 34:23.654
Yes, Mr. Kim.

34:23.654 --> 34:25.823
I checked it like you said.

34:25.823 --> 34:28.158
But do you really

34:28.158 --> 34:29.285
need to know this?

34:29.285 --> 34:30.995
Couldn't you track
the vehicle owner's movements?

34:30.995 --> 34:32.163
Oh, that's not it.

34:32.163 --> 34:33.889
The vehicle belongs to

34:35.916 --> 34:38.018
Han Kyung Wook's secretary.

34:39.169 --> 34:41.505
Han Kyung Wook?

34:41.505 --> 34:43.507
Yes.

34:43.507 --> 34:45.128
[Saehanjin Party, Han Kyung Wook]
Han Kyung Wook, the Saehanjin Party candidate

34:45.128 --> 34:46.818
for Imcheon mayor.

34:49.722 --> 34:50.764
Ma'am,

34:50.764 --> 34:53.225
just drop this case.

34:53.225 --> 34:55.936
You've only just been assigned.

34:55.936 --> 34:57.605
[Hwasan Faction Behind Chief Kwon's Murder]
I'm worried you'll get transferred again.

34:57.605 --> 34:59.648
[Han Kyung Wook uncovered the truth]
I'm saying this out of concern.

34:59.648 --> 35:01.291
And I'm now...

35:04.968 --> 35:06.664
[Han Kyung Wook]

35:11.176 --> 35:13.000
[Han Kyung Wook's Profile]

35:13.000 --> 35:17.352
[Mayoral Candidate Han Kyung Wook, Tourism
is the Way to Save Yeongseondo Island]

35:20.002 --> 35:34.141
- Han Kyung Wook, Han Kyung Wook!
- Han Kyung Wook, Han Kyung Wook!

35:50.658 --> 35:52.993
I ran the motorcycle plate
you mentioned yesterday.

35:52.993 --> 35:54.286
But the owner is

35:54.286 --> 35:58.056
a high school student with no connection
to Bulgae or North Korea.

36:05.381 --> 36:07.732
It's all done. I'll handle it.

36:10.594 --> 36:12.946
Where are you going
in the middle of peeling onions?

36:16.183 --> 36:17.601
Going out to drum up business.

36:17.601 --> 36:18.686
[O Ran Chinese Restaurant]
Need to boost sales, right?

36:18.686 --> 36:19.937
All of a sudden? Hey, hey!

36:19.937 --> 36:21.580
Hey, Jeong Ho Myung!

36:34.410 --> 36:35.869
We'll just check one thing and leave,

36:35.869 --> 36:37.997
so let's avoid making things
awkward for each other.

36:37.997 --> 36:39.415
Don't let Chairman Do hear about this.

36:39.415 --> 36:40.791
You know what I mean?

36:40.791 --> 36:42.042
Yes.

36:42.042 --> 36:45.462
Kang Sik, give him some money for his meds.

36:45.462 --> 36:48.173
Hurry up and find it. Are you playing
a hidden picture game or something?

36:48.173 --> 36:50.843
- Boss.
- Good, Kang Sik found it.

36:50.843 --> 36:52.219
That's not it...

36:52.219 --> 36:54.638
Look here in the lobby, right here.

36:54.638 --> 36:55.973
Isn't that

36:55.973 --> 36:57.641
Ma Gong Bok?

36:57.641 --> 36:59.326
Ma Gong Bok?

37:00.853 --> 37:03.397
Gong Bok showed up after 10 years?

37:03.397 --> 37:05.256
And on this island?

37:05.928 --> 37:06.942
Oh, boss!

37:06.942 --> 37:07.944
Found him!

37:07.944 --> 37:09.544
That's him, that punk!

37:11.530 --> 37:13.131
Oh!

37:17.494 --> 37:19.455
Is that really him?

37:19.455 --> 37:22.249
Looks like he's been wasting away
and can't even put up a fight.

37:22.249 --> 37:24.184
That's definitely him, boss.

37:27.688 --> 37:29.439
Oh, hey, hey!

37:30.632 --> 37:32.426
The guy who crushed our guys

37:32.426 --> 37:35.153
and Gong Bok showed up on the same day?

37:41.832 --> 37:46.056
[Yeongcheon Police Station]

37:47.858 --> 37:49.151
Aren't you going out on patrol?

37:49.151 --> 37:50.344
Huh?

37:50.344 --> 37:51.445
[My cash cow]

37:51.445 --> 37:54.881
Oh, well, go ahead first.

38:03.707 --> 38:05.751
Yeah, I got the call.

38:05.751 --> 38:07.503
Hey, Sergeant Kim. You have been well, right?

38:07.503 --> 38:09.838
It's all thanks to you, sir.

38:09.838 --> 38:11.381
But what's the reason for your call?

38:11.381 --> 38:12.466
Well, at our business site,

38:12.466 --> 38:14.426
a minor problem has come up.

38:14.426 --> 38:16.053
So I need you to look into something.

38:16.053 --> 38:17.513
I'll send you a few photos,

38:17.513 --> 38:19.389
so track down these two guys for me.

38:19.389 --> 38:21.225
Well, if you check the footage

38:21.225 --> 38:23.185
near Heaven Hotel around 3 p.m. yesterday,

38:23.185 --> 38:24.686
tracing their movements shouldn't be hard.

38:24.686 --> 38:27.539
Okay, send me the photos first.

38:30.984 --> 38:32.968
[My cash cow]

38:40.808 --> 38:43.016
[Yeongseon Steel]

39:02.933 --> 39:04.309
Mr. Bong,

39:04.309 --> 39:06.770
what was that unauthorized absence yesterday?

39:06.770 --> 39:07.980
Ms. Lee.

39:07.980 --> 39:10.107
I'm really sorry.

39:10.107 --> 39:12.751
I caused trouble by not showing up
without notice, right?

39:14.361 --> 39:15.946
I covered for you by saying

39:15.946 --> 39:18.490
you already requested leave in advance.

39:18.490 --> 39:20.117
- Ms. Lee...
- You never used to be like this.

39:20.117 --> 39:22.719
You must have had a reason
for not showing up, right?

39:23.537 --> 39:25.998
Thanks. I'll definitely repay you.

39:25.998 --> 39:27.457
But

39:27.457 --> 39:29.585
why were you absent yesterday?

39:29.585 --> 39:31.394
And what's up with your face?

39:32.838 --> 39:34.506
Well,

39:34.506 --> 39:36.383
Ms. Lee, in your opinion,

39:36.383 --> 39:39.261
what kind of work do you think
I did when I was young?

39:39.261 --> 39:40.862
What kind of work?

39:43.362 --> 39:44.994
Well...

39:44.994 --> 39:46.310
Oh!

39:46.310 --> 39:48.061
Weren't you working at a car wash?

39:48.061 --> 39:49.855
You're really good at washing cars.

39:49.855 --> 39:52.540
No, not that.

39:54.401 --> 39:56.361
Look closely.

39:56.361 --> 39:58.071
Nothing comes to mind?

39:58.071 --> 40:01.883
Like I give off a different vibe
or something?

40:03.848 --> 40:05.224
Oh my.

40:15.797 --> 40:17.732
- Mr. Bong.
- Yeah?

40:19.301 --> 40:20.886
- What are you doing?
- I didn't do anything.

40:20.886 --> 40:22.262
Are you crazy?

40:22.262 --> 40:24.197
I'm not crazy though.

40:26.600 --> 40:28.227
Go clean my car.

40:28.227 --> 40:30.145
You didn't clean it yesterday,
so do it properly.

40:30.145 --> 40:31.746
Yes.

40:42.658 --> 40:44.904
Whoa.

40:46.245 --> 40:47.287
How dare he? Huh?

40:47.287 --> 40:49.456
He took leave without my permission?

40:49.456 --> 40:51.917
Mr. Bong, when you take leave,

40:51.917 --> 40:53.919
you need my permission first.

40:53.919 --> 40:55.520
Understand?

41:13.438 --> 41:15.039
Smack!

41:19.945 --> 41:21.613
When the hero's in danger,

41:21.613 --> 41:23.368
their past suddenly flashes back!

41:23.368 --> 41:24.808
Hyah!

41:40.552 --> 41:41.591
Huh?

41:41.591 --> 41:43.568
Boss!

41:55.355 --> 41:57.649
Boss, I'd like to take a half-day off.

41:57.649 --> 41:59.651
- Huh?
- You said I should ask before taking leave.

41:59.651 --> 42:02.003
I'm asking now.

42:04.072 --> 42:05.715
I'll take a half-day off.

42:07.284 --> 42:08.869
Yeah, take it.

42:08.869 --> 42:11.179
Yeah, a half-day off...

42:21.340 --> 42:23.149
Is this really all you've got?

42:23.967 --> 42:26.069
We even take bank transfers.

42:27.387 --> 42:28.555
Answer carefully.

42:28.555 --> 42:30.531
Hey guys,

42:32.642 --> 42:33.894
can I ask something?

42:33.894 --> 42:35.979
What? I'm busy, can't you see?

42:35.979 --> 42:38.148
Doesn't look that busy to me.

42:38.148 --> 42:39.816
Enough with the thug act.

42:39.816 --> 42:41.860
Just answer my question.

42:41.860 --> 42:42.903
Who is

42:42.903 --> 42:45.004
Kim Jin Soo here?

42:48.200 --> 42:49.801
That's me.

42:54.498 --> 42:56.432
Kim Jin Soo.

42:58.460 --> 43:01.380
It's not the guy who was
riding the motorcycle.

43:01.380 --> 43:05.217
Oh, so you're Jin Soo.

43:05.217 --> 43:07.386
- Jin Soo!
- Yeah.

43:07.386 --> 43:08.804
You've got a motorcycle, right?

43:08.804 --> 43:10.430
Did you lend it to someone?

43:10.430 --> 43:11.723
Why should I tell you that?

43:11.723 --> 43:13.016
Could you tell me?

43:13.016 --> 43:14.559
I really need to know.

43:14.559 --> 43:16.895
If you really need to know,

43:16.895 --> 43:18.438
you should offer something in return.

43:18.438 --> 43:20.039
You think I'll just talk for free?

43:21.900 --> 43:23.501
Grab him!

43:25.279 --> 43:27.030
Oh, wow.

43:27.030 --> 43:29.074
Okay, if what comes out
of you is good enough,

43:29.074 --> 43:31.243
I'll let you know what you want.

43:31.243 --> 43:32.577
Oh dear, what to do?

43:32.577 --> 43:34.871
I have no money.

43:34.871 --> 43:36.806
But I can give you something else.

43:45.715 --> 43:48.067
- Jin Soo!
- Hey.

43:50.178 --> 43:53.992
Hey, what are you doing? Hurry up! Darn it.

44:04.151 --> 44:05.793
Ouch, it hurts!

44:11.533 --> 44:13.326
When an adult asks a question,

44:13.326 --> 44:14.619
you should answer!

44:14.619 --> 44:17.038
- Where are your manners, huh?
- Ugh, sir!

44:17.038 --> 44:18.915
- It hurts, it hurts!
- How dare you throw a punch?

44:18.915 --> 44:20.041
Sir!

44:20.041 --> 44:21.543
Sir, it hurts!

44:21.543 --> 44:23.227
Ugh, it hurts, it hurts!

44:28.758 --> 44:30.677
- Jin Soo!
- Yes.

44:30.677 --> 44:33.221
- I'll ask one more time.
- Yeah.

44:33.221 --> 44:34.723
You've got a motorcycle, right?

44:34.723 --> 44:35.974
That flashy one.

44:35.974 --> 44:38.701
- My scooter?
- Yeah, that one.

44:39.519 --> 44:41.354
Heo Nam Il, that guy took it.

44:41.354 --> 44:42.731
Why?

44:42.731 --> 44:44.582
- Heo Nam Il?
- Yeah.

44:47.861 --> 44:50.797
Is that punk trying to drive me insane?

44:54.910 --> 44:55.994
Huh?

44:55.994 --> 44:57.595
Orthostatic...

45:19.017 --> 45:20.743
Are you alright?

45:22.020 --> 45:23.621
Sorry.

45:26.066 --> 45:27.834
When did you get here?

45:28.735 --> 45:30.987
I just got here.

45:30.987 --> 45:32.197
[Police]
But are you feeling unwell?

45:32.197 --> 45:33.990
No, well...

45:33.990 --> 45:35.909
Oh, I haven't been

45:35.909 --> 45:38.245
sleeping well lately.

45:38.245 --> 45:39.846
I'm sorry.

45:48.338 --> 45:49.881
The lunchbox is over there, right?

45:49.881 --> 45:50.882
Lunchbox? Oh, yes.

45:50.882 --> 45:53.192
J-Just a moment please.

46:01.226 --> 46:02.978
[Sweet and Sour Soy Chicken Lunchbox]
Huh? It's the sweet and sour soy chicken?

46:02.978 --> 46:04.579
Yes.

46:13.863 --> 46:15.907
Oh.

46:15.907 --> 46:18.493
Don't feel pressured.

46:18.493 --> 46:19.661
Fortunately, they had

46:19.661 --> 46:21.162
what you mentioned last time in stock,

46:21.162 --> 46:24.291
so I was curious myself
and went ahead and placed an order.

46:24.291 --> 46:26.209
Well,

46:26.209 --> 46:28.895
oh, this is a special service for regulars.

46:32.549 --> 46:34.901
You said you haven't been
sleeping well, right?

46:36.177 --> 46:38.487
Could you give me your hand?

46:43.143 --> 46:45.437
Not like when handcuffs...

46:45.437 --> 46:47.371
M-My arm's just numb...

46:47.981 --> 46:49.665
No, like this.

46:55.739 --> 46:59.826
This is what I eat during night patrols.

46:59.826 --> 47:02.303
It actually works pretty well.

47:03.246 --> 47:05.957
Eat it and try to freshen up a bit.

47:05.957 --> 47:07.558
Yes.

47:10.128 --> 47:11.921
Thank you.

47:11.921 --> 47:13.522
And thank you as well.

47:21.056 --> 47:22.657
Goodbye.

47:23.308 --> 47:24.909
Take care.

47:51.711 --> 47:53.354
She said thank you.

48:05.642 --> 48:07.243
What?

48:14.567 --> 48:16.236
I rushed over

48:16.236 --> 48:17.904
because you said

48:17.904 --> 48:19.906
you couldn't sleep and felt like dying.

48:19.906 --> 48:22.659
- But you seem totally fine.
- Can't you see my dark circles?

48:22.659 --> 48:24.953
Enough. Just call it a day.

48:24.953 --> 48:26.538
You must be exhausted from everything.

48:26.538 --> 48:28.540
Who was the one who dumped everything

48:28.540 --> 48:30.834
and ran off first?

48:30.834 --> 48:33.378
Did I go out and mess around like you?

48:33.378 --> 48:35.338
You don't even care about our work!

48:35.338 --> 48:37.716
Our real job!

48:37.716 --> 48:41.052
I handled it while you were
flirting with that woman!

48:41.052 --> 48:42.987
You punk!

48:49.144 --> 48:50.562
Alright.

48:50.562 --> 48:52.605
Hit me.

48:52.605 --> 48:54.315
I want to take a solid hit after so long.

48:54.315 --> 48:55.859
Hit me!

48:55.859 --> 48:57.460
Go on!

49:03.199 --> 49:04.242
Let's cool off

49:04.242 --> 49:06.052
and talk later.

49:08.913 --> 49:11.015
You can't even hit me anymore?

49:12.459 --> 49:14.335
You know,

49:14.335 --> 49:16.796
compared to the friendly convenience store
owner Kang Beom Ryong,

49:16.796 --> 49:20.175
I miss Kang Beom Ryong of Hwasan faction,

49:20.175 --> 49:23.178
the boss who used to charge ahead
without thinking.

49:23.178 --> 49:24.779
Not working, darn it.

49:28.224 --> 49:29.825
Jeez!

49:44.073 --> 49:45.533
Gong Bok, Beom Ryong, those punks.

49:45.533 --> 49:47.160
After ten years,

49:47.160 --> 49:49.261
they finally show up
just to ruin my business?

49:49.871 --> 49:52.223
We should've taken them out back then.

49:54.459 --> 49:56.127
But boss,

49:56.127 --> 49:58.296
do you think the guy who caused all this

49:58.296 --> 49:59.881
is actually connected

49:59.881 --> 50:01.925
to Boss Beom Ryong and Gong Bok?

50:01.925 --> 50:05.069
You punk, how dare you still call him "boss"?

50:05.762 --> 50:07.639
Listen.

50:07.639 --> 50:09.349
Do you really think it's a coincidence

50:09.349 --> 50:12.060
that Gong Bok showed up right
when you were getting beaten?

50:12.060 --> 50:13.144
That punk Kang Beom Ryong

50:13.144 --> 50:14.187
must have hired

50:14.187 --> 50:15.939
some martial arts expert or whatever

50:15.939 --> 50:18.791
to come after me after I took down
Chairman Hwang Hwa San.

50:19.442 --> 50:20.985
He can't fight me one-on-one anymore,

50:20.985 --> 50:23.045
so he's using guys like this instead?

50:26.616 --> 50:28.660
This scar aches when it rains.

50:28.660 --> 50:31.454
I think it's finally time for revenge.

50:31.454 --> 50:33.790
Boss, Sergeant Kim just called!

50:33.790 --> 50:35.083
He has located both of them.

50:35.083 --> 50:36.876
Okay! Everyone get ready!

50:36.876 --> 50:38.602
- Yes!
- Yes!

50:43.633 --> 50:44.926
Let's move out!

50:44.926 --> 50:46.986
- Yes!
- Yes!

50:50.765 --> 50:52.366
So,

50:53.518 --> 50:55.228
you got hit once and your memory came back?

50:55.228 --> 50:56.855
No, no, before getting hit.

50:56.855 --> 50:58.690
I felt a baseball coming from behind,

50:58.690 --> 51:02.376
and suddenly a scene flashed through my head.

51:03.278 --> 51:05.045
Back when I was young,

51:05.655 --> 51:08.408
I had these rock-hard abs.

51:08.408 --> 51:09.868
And I kicked away

51:09.868 --> 51:12.036
a flying dagger coming from behind
with my legs.

51:12.036 --> 51:13.621
Oh, please, kicking a dagger away?

51:13.621 --> 51:15.290
It's true!

51:15.290 --> 51:17.808
Try it, I'll...

51:19.752 --> 51:21.838
Come on.

51:21.838 --> 51:23.856
I'll sense it and dodge.

51:34.088 --> 51:35.184
Huh? Boss!

51:35.184 --> 51:36.185
- Is he here?
- Yes, he is.

51:36.185 --> 51:37.312
Hey, get inside, get inside, hurry!

51:37.312 --> 51:39.497
Get inside, now! Move! Go!

51:41.232 --> 51:43.318
Ha, you little punk!

51:43.318 --> 51:45.361
Here you are, huh?

51:45.361 --> 51:47.213
What's this? Are you greeting us?

51:50.082 --> 51:51.336
Well.

51:53.453 --> 51:54.621
What's going on?

51:54.621 --> 51:57.540
- What?
- What? Why?

51:57.540 --> 51:58.625
No, it's not that, well...

51:58.625 --> 52:00.267
Hold on a second.

52:00.267 --> 52:01.480
- Oh!
- Hey, you scared me!

52:01.480 --> 52:02.536
What's going on?

52:02.536 --> 52:05.022
Did he know we were coming or what?

52:08.927 --> 52:10.528
Just a moment...

52:11.137 --> 52:13.113
Wait!

52:20.313 --> 52:21.439
Darn, you scared me.

52:21.439 --> 52:22.690
Grab him!

52:22.690 --> 52:24.317
Hey, grab that punk!

52:24.317 --> 52:25.918
You startled me!

52:34.869 --> 52:37.012
Welcome to Jumbo Convenience Store...

52:54.180 --> 52:56.156
Gong Bok, it's been a while.

53:15.080 --> 53:18.386
[O Ran Chinese Restaurant]

53:35.054 --> 53:37.281
Your jjajang noodles have arrived!

53:38.850 --> 53:40.743
I'll come in!

54:14.761 --> 54:16.596
Seeing how messy the house is,

54:16.596 --> 54:19.198
someone might've gotten here first.

54:23.394 --> 54:25.996
Yeongseon Steel.

54:31.402 --> 54:34.963
Yeongseon... Food.

54:45.124 --> 54:46.459
You know,

54:46.459 --> 54:49.212
compared to the friendly convenience store
owner Kang Beom Ryong,

54:49.212 --> 54:52.632
I miss Kang Beom Ryong of Hwasan faction,

54:52.632 --> 54:55.859
the boss who used to charge ahead
without thinking.

55:01.026 --> 55:03.031
Darn it!

55:13.960 --> 55:15.283
[1 Unread Message]

55:21.512 --> 55:25.123
[Ma Gong Bok]

55:25.123 --> 55:26.332
Hey, Gong Bok.

55:26.332 --> 55:27.834
Oh, my, Beom Ryong!

55:27.834 --> 55:29.416
It's been a while.

55:29.416 --> 55:30.503
Who are you?

55:30.503 --> 55:32.672
Oh, dear. Have you forgotten my voice?

55:32.672 --> 55:34.215
That hurts.

55:34.215 --> 55:35.858
It's me, In Goo.

55:37.544 --> 55:38.594
How did you...

55:38.594 --> 55:40.471
Since we're all old Hwasan faction family,

55:40.471 --> 55:42.431
we should catch up.

55:42.431 --> 55:44.600
I'll text you the meeting place.

55:44.600 --> 55:46.602
So don't be late.

55:46.602 --> 55:49.063
I'm dying to see your face.

55:49.063 --> 55:51.707
Beom Ryong, please save me!

55:57.992 --> 56:00.840
[Don't make me any more furious]

56:45.369 --> 56:47.914
Now it's confirmed.

56:47.914 --> 56:49.890
The guy in this house

56:56.631 --> 56:59.217
is the missing Bulgae!

56:59.217 --> 57:02.720
Oh, sir. It's not like I'm asking you
to do something impossible.

57:02.720 --> 57:04.513
I'm just asking you to look into someone

57:04.513 --> 57:06.312
who used to work
with Deputy Director Han Kyung Wook.

57:06.312 --> 57:07.400
What's so difficult about that?

57:07.400 --> 57:09.227
Do you want me dead?

57:09.227 --> 57:11.938
Han Kyung Wook came from our company.

57:11.938 --> 57:14.315
Do you think there's anywhere
in the company he doesn't have connections?

57:14.315 --> 57:16.192
He left when he entered politics.

57:16.192 --> 57:17.735
So his ties must be gone by now.

57:17.735 --> 57:19.278
They're still very strong.

57:19.278 --> 57:20.404
Gotta go now.

57:20.404 --> 57:22.573
- Don't get me in trouble too.
- No, wait, wait!

57:22.573 --> 57:23.991
Just one question, just one!

57:23.991 --> 57:25.243
Only one.

57:25.243 --> 57:27.078
Get up, get up!

57:27.078 --> 57:28.537
Jeez, you punk.

57:28.537 --> 57:30.138
What's up with you punk?

57:34.335 --> 57:36.812
Come on, are you going to talk or not?

57:37.797 --> 57:39.857
What's your relationship with him?

57:40.508 --> 57:42.802
I'm just his uncle...

57:42.802 --> 57:45.070
Still not talking, huh?

57:45.721 --> 57:47.139
Then I've got no choice.

57:47.139 --> 57:49.976
I'm going to ask questions now.

57:49.976 --> 57:51.644
If your answers are unsatisfactory,

57:51.644 --> 57:53.104
or you rub me the wrong way,

57:53.104 --> 57:55.314
then you better be ready to get wrecked.

57:55.314 --> 57:57.624
Think carefully before you answer.

57:59.402 --> 58:01.737
You punk, get up!

58:01.737 --> 58:03.922
Gong Bok, you go first.

58:04.865 --> 58:07.159
You punk, why did you suddenly show up here?

58:07.159 --> 58:10.246
I was just chilling at the convenience store!

58:10.246 --> 58:11.872
You're the one
who suddenly showed up, not me.

58:11.872 --> 58:12.999
Yoo In Goo, you punk!

58:12.999 --> 58:14.975
Have you lost your mind?

58:16.002 --> 58:18.671
Gong Bok, let's think about this rationally.

58:18.671 --> 58:20.006
At this critical time

58:20.006 --> 58:22.925
when I'm running a new business
in Yeongseondo Island,

58:22.925 --> 58:24.844
you showed up

58:24.844 --> 58:26.304
right after that punk

58:26.304 --> 58:28.597
destroyed my business, Heaven Capital.

58:28.597 --> 58:31.100
And you still claim to be just
a harmless convenience store clerk?

58:31.100 --> 58:33.102
And this is all just a coincidence?

58:33.102 --> 58:34.353
Do you think that makes sense?

58:34.353 --> 58:37.289
I don't know anything about it, you punk!

58:39.066 --> 58:41.110
Your answer is unsatisfactory.

58:41.110 --> 58:42.711
Help him up!

58:44.447 --> 58:46.173
Alright, hurry up.

58:50.036 --> 58:51.162
Help him up!

58:51.162 --> 58:53.831
You punk!

58:53.831 --> 58:55.515
Take that!

58:56.765 --> 58:59.068
Oh, my.

59:29.608 --> 59:31.928
[Two NIS agents vanished
during a ferry arrest operation]

59:31.928 --> 59:33.512
[before making contact with North Korea]

59:34.663 --> 59:36.374
Ten years ago,

59:36.374 --> 59:38.918
the ferry incident where NIS agents

59:38.918 --> 59:41.462
were colluding with spies?

59:41.462 --> 59:42.463
Yes.

59:42.463 --> 59:44.298
Who was in charge

59:44.298 --> 59:46.525
of that case?

59:47.176 --> 59:48.928
First Deputy Director Han Kyung Wook.

59:48.928 --> 59:50.612
Han Kyung Wook?

59:51.639 --> 59:53.391
Oh, if it's Han Kyung Wook,

59:53.391 --> 59:56.018
he also caught the killer

59:56.018 --> 59:58.646
in the Chief Kwon Sun Bok murder case

59:58.646 --> 01:00:00.606
around the same time,

01:00:00.606 --> 01:00:02.088
so are these two cases somewhat connected?

01:00:02.088 --> 01:00:04.485
I can't say any more.

01:00:04.485 --> 01:00:08.155
The higher-ups have put this under wraps.

01:00:08.155 --> 01:00:10.741
This is on a completely different level

01:00:10.741 --> 01:00:12.576
from anything you've handled before.

01:00:12.576 --> 01:00:15.178
[Chairman Hwang Hwa San]
Stop here before things get bloody.

01:00:21.252 --> 01:00:23.228
Yep, Mr. Kim.

01:00:23.880 --> 01:00:25.005
What?

01:00:25.005 --> 01:00:27.425
I mean, a car suddenly crossed lanes

01:00:27.425 --> 01:00:29.093
and just rammed me and drove off.

01:00:29.093 --> 01:00:30.094
What about the vehicle that hit you?

01:00:30.094 --> 01:00:32.721
We ran the license plate,

01:00:32.721 --> 01:00:34.515
but it's fake.

01:00:34.515 --> 01:00:36.575
A fake plate?

01:00:39.019 --> 01:00:40.271
Uncle!

01:00:40.271 --> 01:00:41.772
This is an emergency.

01:00:41.772 --> 01:00:44.358
Call agent 007!

01:00:44.358 --> 01:00:46.710
I don't know, just be quiet.

01:00:50.322 --> 01:00:51.907
Wait.

01:00:51.907 --> 01:00:53.868
Do you need to get hit for it to come out?

01:00:53.868 --> 01:00:54.952
Are you crazy?

01:00:54.952 --> 01:00:57.037
You want me to get hit?

01:00:57.037 --> 01:00:59.165
- It stills hurts here.
- Hey.

01:00:59.165 --> 01:01:00.291
You're next,

01:01:00.291 --> 01:01:02.642
so shut your mouths.

01:01:10.134 --> 01:01:13.387
Jeez, this stubborn guy won't
open his mouth till the end.

01:01:13.387 --> 01:01:16.182
You're dead when Beom Ryong
gets here, you punk.

01:01:16.182 --> 01:01:18.726
Oh, I've checked.

01:01:18.726 --> 01:01:22.062
Mr. Kang Beom Ryong has run
a convenience store for ten years.

01:01:22.062 --> 01:01:24.440
He's scanned barcodes for ten years.

01:01:24.440 --> 01:01:26.583
Do you think he still has his old moves?

01:01:53.093 --> 01:01:55.513
Alright, let's move on to the next one.

01:01:55.513 --> 01:01:57.447
Hey, Mr. Martial Arts Master!

01:01:58.807 --> 01:02:01.227
Is it true you were paid
to beat our guys to a pulp?

01:02:01.227 --> 01:02:02.728
Oh, sir.

01:02:02.728 --> 01:02:03.771
What do you mean "paid"?

01:02:03.771 --> 01:02:04.855
I'm just...

01:02:04.855 --> 01:02:06.899
an ordinary office worker, really.

01:02:06.899 --> 01:02:08.526
Just a regular office worker.

01:02:08.526 --> 01:02:11.237
He's not a martial arts master,
but more like a comedian?

01:02:11.237 --> 01:02:12.488
Is it true you got beat up by this punk?

01:02:12.488 --> 01:02:13.948
It's true, boss.

01:02:13.948 --> 01:02:16.283
I mean, that guy got
knocked out after one punch,

01:02:16.283 --> 01:02:18.494
then suddenly got up like a zombie,

01:02:18.494 --> 01:02:19.537
rolled his eyes,

01:02:19.537 --> 01:02:21.680
and caused all that mess, really.

01:02:22.998 --> 01:02:24.599
E-Excuse me...

01:02:25.668 --> 01:02:27.769
Give him a punch.

01:02:28.712 --> 01:02:30.047
Try punching him once.

01:02:30.047 --> 01:02:32.508
- Are you insane?
- What, is he the Hulk who can transform?

01:02:32.508 --> 01:02:34.426
No, no, sir. It's not that, this guy...

01:02:34.426 --> 01:02:35.678
Are you crazy?

01:02:35.678 --> 01:02:36.680
It's okay, Uncle.

01:02:36.680 --> 01:02:38.472
These guys are having fun, huh?

01:02:38.472 --> 01:02:40.240
Hey, try hitting this punk.

01:02:42.142 --> 01:02:43.477
Is it really okay?

01:02:43.477 --> 01:02:46.079
- Should I do it?
- No, I'll do it.

01:02:51.193 --> 01:02:52.945
You scared me! Scared me!

01:02:52.945 --> 01:02:54.405
You punk, you startled me!

01:02:54.405 --> 01:02:56.574
You punk, you call that a punch?

01:02:56.574 --> 01:02:59.134
- Hit harder! Harder!
- It's hard enough.

01:03:01.120 --> 01:03:02.721
Uncle!

01:03:09.670 --> 01:03:11.422
Uncle!

01:03:11.422 --> 01:03:13.023
He's out!

01:03:14.633 --> 01:03:16.260
It hurts too much.

01:03:16.260 --> 01:03:17.861
It hurts too much.

01:03:19.471 --> 01:03:21.072
Uncle...

01:03:23.309 --> 01:03:24.910
Uncle!

01:03:27.187 --> 01:03:28.522
I said it hurts too much!

01:03:28.522 --> 01:03:31.499
I've told you several times
I'm just an ordinary office worker...

01:03:32.318 --> 01:03:34.361
- Hey, step on him!
- Step on him!

01:03:34.361 --> 01:03:35.962
Wait...

01:04:02.681 --> 01:04:03.932
Hey, Gong Bok!

01:04:03.932 --> 01:04:06.727
Did your fancy convenience store boss
run away?

01:04:06.727 --> 01:04:08.020
Why isn't he coming?

01:04:08.020 --> 01:04:09.313
Huh?

01:04:09.313 --> 01:04:12.290
I need revenge for this scar!

01:04:19.990 --> 01:04:22.201
There's no choice.

01:04:22.201 --> 01:04:24.161
Can't get the main target,
so I'll just settle for the secondary.

01:04:24.161 --> 01:04:26.471
I'll have to take it out on you.

01:04:43.764 --> 01:04:45.365
What was that?

01:04:47.592 --> 01:04:48.769
No!

01:04:48.769 --> 01:04:50.938
Hey, grab him!

01:04:50.938 --> 01:04:52.956
Stop, stop!

01:05:30.060 --> 01:05:31.953
Beom Ryong!

01:05:34.398 --> 01:05:36.583
- That punk Kang Beom Ryong!
- Come on.

01:05:38.026 --> 01:05:39.737
I haven't slept in two days,

01:05:39.737 --> 01:05:41.671
so I'm darn tired.

01:05:42.364 --> 01:05:43.965
Gong Bok,

01:05:45.534 --> 01:05:47.552
let's wrap this up quickly and go.

01:06:12.099 --> 01:06:14.152
What are you really trying to do?

01:06:14.152 --> 01:06:15.816
You think I chose to live like this?

01:06:15.816 --> 01:06:18.544
This is all your fault, Jeong Ho Myung!

01:06:18.544 --> 01:06:21.000
Citizens who work hard like you

01:06:21.000 --> 01:06:22.856
need cops like me to protect them.

01:06:24.494 --> 01:06:30.184
Even the purest water turns muddy
after a few rainstorms.

01:06:30.184 --> 01:06:31.720
I don't understand, why?

01:06:31.720 --> 01:06:34.056
Something feels off. I smell something fishy.

01:06:34.056 --> 01:06:36.418
Be careful.
It's your first mission in ten years.

01:06:36.418 --> 01:06:39.688
Hey, what's wrong?
Have you forgotten who I am?

01:06:39.688 --> 01:06:43.432
That guy, believe it or not,
